### Create and Use a Scalar UDF Expression

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/docs/source/library-user-guide/working-with-exprs.md

Demonstrates how to define a scalar UDF and then use it to create expressions involving literals and column references. Ensure the UDF logic is defined elsewhere.

```rust
use datafusion::logical_expr::{Volatility, create_udf};
use datafusion::arrow::datatypes::DataType;
use datafusion::logical_expr::{col, lit};

let add_one_udf = create_udf(
    "add_one",
    vec![DataType::Int64],
    DataType::Int64,
    Volatility::Immutable,
    Arc::new(add_one),
);

// make the expr `add_one(5)`
let expr = add_one_udf.call(vec![lit(5)]);

// make the expr `add_one(my_column)`
let expr = add_one_udf.call(vec![col("my_column")]);
```

