### Implement a Scalar UDF in Rust

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/docs/source/library-user-guide/functions/adding-udfs.md

Defines a function that accepts ColumnarValue arguments and returns a transformed array.

```rust
use std::sync::Arc;
use datafusion::arrow::array::{ArrayRef, Int64Array};
use datafusion::common::cast::as_int64_array;
use datafusion::common::Result;
use datafusion::logical_expr::ColumnarValue;

pub fn add_one(args: &[ColumnarValue]) -> Result<ColumnarValue> {
    // Error handling omitted for brevity
    let args = ColumnarValue::values_to_arrays(args)?;
    let i64s = as_int64_array(&args[0])?;

    let new_array = i64s
        .iter()
        .map(|array_elem| array_elem.map(|value| value + 1))
        .collect::<Int64Array>();

    Ok(ColumnarValue::from(Arc::new(new_array) as ArrayRef))
}
```

### Adding a Scalar UDF by create_udf > Registering a Scalar UDF

Source: https://github.com/apache/datafusion/blob/main/docs/source/library-user-guide/functions/adding-udfs.md

When using create_udf, you must specify the function name for SQL usage, the expected input data types, the return data type, and the function's volatility. Volatility is critical for query optimization; for example, an Immutable function always returns the same output for a given input, whereas a Volatile function, such as a random number generator, may return different results for the same input.

### Query Delta Table with DataFusion SQL API (Rust)

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/docs/usage/querying-delta-tables.md

Query a Delta table using Apache DataFusion's SQL interface in Rust. This requires setting up a DataFusion session context and registering the Delta table. Requires `deltalake` and `datafusion`.

```rust
use url::Url;
use deltalake::open_table;
use datafusion::prelude::SessionContext;

let delta_path = Url::from_directory_path("/rust/tests/data/delta-0.8.0-partitioned").unwrap();
let table = open_table(delta_path).await?;
let ctx = SessionContext::new();
ctx.register_table("simple_table", table.table_provider().await?)?;
let df = ctx.sql("SELECT value FROM simple_table WHERE year = 2021").await?;
df.show().await?;
```

