### Delete Rows Using Rust with Datafusion Expression

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/docs/usage/deleting-rows-from-delta-lake-table.md

In Rust, use the `DeltaOps` trait to delete rows. The `with_predicate` method accepts an expression that can be translated to a Datafusion `Expression`, allowing for programmatic filtering.

```Rust
let delta_path = Url::from_directory_path("/tmp/some-table").unwrap();
let mut table = open_table(delta_path).await?;
let (table, delete_metrics) = DeltaOps(table)
    .delete()
    .with_predicate(col("num").gt(lit(2)))
    .await?;
```

