### Perform Insert Merge Operation (Rust)

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/docs/usage/merging-tables.md

Executes a merge operation to insert new records into the target Delta table using Rust. Only rows not present in the target based on the predicate are inserted.

```rust
DeltaOps(table)
.merge(source_data, "target.x = source.x")
.with_source_alias("source")
.with_target_alias("target")
.when_not_matched_insert(
    |insert| insert.set("x", "source.x").set("y", "source.y")
)?.await?;
```

### Transaction (txn) action struct — JSON fields of SetTransaction

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/crates/core/src/kernel/models/actions.rs

Defines the `Transaction` action struct that backs the `txn` entry in `_delta_log` JSON files. With `#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]` it serializes to `{"txn":{"appId":"<string>","version":<int>,"lastUpdated":<long ms>}}`, where appId is the application identifier, version is the application-specific numeric version, and lastUpdated (optional) is the creation time in milliseconds since the Unix epoch. It also provides the constructors used by the SetTransaction writer (`Transaction::new` and `new_with_last_update`).

```rust
/// Action used by streaming systems to track progress using application-specific versions to
/// enable idempotency.
#[derive(Serialize, Deserialize, Debug, Default, Clone, PartialEq, Eq)]
#[serde(rename_all = "camelCase")]
pub struct Transaction {
    /// A unique identifier for the application performing the transaction.
    pub app_id: String,

    /// An application-specific numeric identifier for this transaction.
    pub version: i64,

    /// The time when this transaction action was created in milliseconds since the Unix epoch.
    #[serde(skip_serializing_if = "Option::is_none")]
    pub last_updated: Option<i64>,
}

impl Transaction {
    /// Create a new application transactions. See [`Txn`] for details.
    pub fn new(app_id: impl ToString, version: i64) -> Self {
        Self::new_with_last_update(app_id, version, None)
    }

    /// Create a new application transactions. See [`Txn`] for details.
    pub fn new_with_last_update(
        app_id: impl ToString,
        version: i64,
        last_updated: Option<i64>,
    ) -> Self {
        Transaction {
            app_id: app_id.to_string(),
            version,
            last_updated,
        }
    }
}
```

