### Why Delta Lake depends on DataFusion

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/docs/integrations/delta-lake-datafusion.md

Delta Lake relies on DataFusion for implementing several end-user features that involve SQL expressions, such as update and merge operations, as well as defining invariants and constraints. DataFusion acts as the underlying SQL engine for evaluating these expressions.

--------------------------------

### Delta Lake Best Practices > Use appropriate quality controls

Source: https://github.com/delta-io/delta-rs/blob/main/docs/usage/delta-lake-best-practices.md

Delta Lake enforces schema by default, ensuring data appended to a table matches its existing schema. Schema evolution can be enabled to allow schema changes, but should only be used when this flexibility is desired. Column-level constraints can be added to enforce specific data predicates, preventing rows that fail the constraint from being appended.
